hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27923","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Abu al-Nadr, from Abu Murrah, the freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, from Umm Hani, that she went to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of the conquest. She said: I found him bathing, with Fatimah screening him with a garment. I greeted, and that was forenoon. He said: Who is this. I said: I am Umm Hani. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the son of my mother claims that he will kill a man I granted protection, Fulan ibn Hubayrah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We have granted protection to whom you granted protection, O Umm Hani. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his washing, he stood and prayed eight rakahs, wrapped in a garment."
"27924","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Said, from Abu Murrah, the freedman of Aqil, from Umm Hani, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at upper Makkah, and I did not find him, and I found Fatimah. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, with the trace of dust upon him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have granted protection to two of my in-laws, and the son of my mother claims that he will kill them. He said: We have granted protection to whom you granted protection. Washing was placed for him in a bowl, and I saw the trace of dough therein. He performed ablution, or he said: He bathed; I doubt; and he prayed Fajr in a garment, wrapped therein."
"27925","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take sheep, for therein is blessing."
"27926","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us: Misar narrated to us, from Abu al-Ala al-Abdi, from Ibn Jadah ibn Hubayrah, from Umm Hani, she said: I used to hear the recitation of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while I was upon my trellis."
"27927","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Abi Sagheerah informed me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Salih, the freedman of Umm Hani, from Umm Hani, she said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about His saying, Exalted is He: And you commit evil in your clubs. He said: They used to pelt the people of the road and mock them, and that is the evil which they used to commit."
"27928","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Harun, the son of the daughter of Umm Hani, or the son of Umm Hani, from Umm Hani, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to me and asked for drink, and he was given drink and drank, then he handed me his remainder, and I drank. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I was fasting, but I disliked to return your leftover. He said: Were you making up anything. I said: No. He said: Then there is no harm upon you."
"27929","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Abu Yunus al-Qushayri Hatim ibn Abi Sagheerah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abu Salih, from Umm Hani, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to her on the day of the conquest, and she brought him drink, and he drank from it, then there remained of it a remainder, and he handed it to her, and she drank it. Then she said: O Messenger of Allah, I did something, I do not know whether it pleases you or not. He said: And what is that, O Umm Hani. She said: I was fasting, but I disliked to return your remainder, so I drank it. He said: Voluntary or obligatory. She said: I said: Rather voluntary. He said: Then the voluntary faster has the choice: if he wishes, he fasts, and if he wishes, he breaks fast."
"27930","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, he said: Yusuf ibn Mahak narrated to me that he entered upon Umm Hani bint Abi Talib and asked her about the entrance of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of the conquest. He asked her: Did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray with you. She said: He entered in the forenoon, and I poured for him water in a bowl of ours; I indeed see therein the bran of dough. Yusuf said: I do not know which of that she informed me: he performed ablution or he bathed. Then he bowed in this mosque, a mosque in her house, four rakahs. Yusuf said: So I stood and performed ablution from a waterskin of hers, and prayed in that mosque four rakahs."
"27931","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Aswad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Nawfal narrated to us that he heard Durrah bint Muadh narrating from Umm Hani, that she asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Shall we visit one another when we die, and some of us see others. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Souls shall be birds clinging to trees, until when they are on the Day of Resurrection, every soul shall enter its body."
"27932","Ishaq narrated to us: Malik informed me, from Abu al-Nadr, that Abu Murrah, the freedman of Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, informed him that he heard Umm Hani saying: I went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the year of the conquest, and I found him bathing, with Fatimah his daughter screening him with a garment. She said: I greeted. He said: Who is this. He said: She said: Umm Hani bint Abi Talib. He said: Welcome to Umm Hani. She said: When he finished his washing, he stood and prayed eight rakahs, wrapped in a single garment. Then he turned, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, the son of my mother claims that he will kill a man I granted protection, Fulan ibn Hubayrah. He said: We have granted protection to whom you granted protection, O Umm Hani. Umm Hani said: And that was forenoon."
"27933","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to Makkah once, and he had four braids."
"27934","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Najih mentioning, from Mujahid, from Umm Hani, she said: I saw upon the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, four plaits."
"27935","Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, he said: I asked him about the forenoon prayer. He said: I asked the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about it, and I did not find anyone informing me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed it, except that Umm Hani informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her and prayed eight rakahs, and I never saw him pray before it nor after it."
"27936","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Musa ibn Maysarah, from Abu Murrah, that he heard Umm Hani saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in my house eight rakahs, in a single garment, wrapped therein."
"27937","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from Salih, the freedman of Wajzah, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman grown heavy, so teach me something I may say while sitting. He said: Say: Allah is Greatest, a hundred times, for it is better for you than a hundred adorned accepted camels. And say: Praise be to Allah, a hundred times, for it is better for you than a hundred saddled bridled horses you carry in the path of Allah. And say: Glory be to Allah, a hundred times; it is better for you than a hundred necks of the children of Ismail you free. And say: There is no god but Allah, a hundred times; it leaves no sin, nor is it preceded by deed."
